course: dictionary
lesson: 5357
title: Kindness in words and actions
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Kindness is a noun, and it is usually uncountable: you show kindness, you do not collect many of them. Kindness means being friendly, caring and helpful to others. It is something you show through what you do.
explain: Read the clues around the word. «Kindness is small and quick online: inviting someone who always plays alone, saying "nice one", or being an upstander.» These examples are small things that help someone, so kindness does not have to be big. An upstander is someone who supports a person being bullied and tells an adult.
explain: A kindness is one kind act, and it can be countable. «Giving is not only money; a volunteer helps without being paid, and time, help and kindness count too.» Here kindness sits beside time and help, so it is something you give to other people.
explain: Kindness is the opposite of bullying, and it makes people feel safe and happy. «Compliment things people choose, like their drawing, kindness or effort, rather than their body or weight.» Praising what someone does is a kind way to make them feel good.
fact: Kindness means being friendly, caring and helpful to others.
fact: A kindness is a kind act, so you can talk about several kindnesses.
fact: «Random acts of kindness» are small kind things done for anyone.
fact: Kindness makes people feel safe and happy, and it is the opposite of bullying.
fact: In fairy tales, kindness is often rewarded, like the kind girl who helps an old woman.
exercise: «Compliment things people choose, like their drawing, kindness or effort, rather than their body or weight.» Which compliment is kind? | You are very heavy for your age | You look skinny today | *You worked so hard on this drawing | Your hair is too messy
exercise: Which of these is an example of a kindness, one kind act? | Telling a secret about a friend | Ignoring a classmate who is hurt | *Inviting someone who always plays alone to join your game | Calling someone a name online
exercise: What is an upstander? | Someone who never speaks up at all | Someone who tells jokes about other people | Someone who joins in when others are mean | *Someone who supports a person being bullied and tells an adult
test: Which word means being friendly, caring and helpful to others? | *Kindness | Snitching | Upstander | Bullying
test: «Respect is earned by effort, skill, honesty, kindness and courage.» Which word is NOT on that list? | *Strength | Effort | Honesty | Courage
exam: Kindness makes people feel safe and happy, and it is the opposite of which word? | *Bullying | Sharing | Helping | Saying thank you
